!! 2 · The cache story (the setting the house changed on 2026-10-28)

| era | model | role | n | cache write : read | calls writing > 50k tok | tokens in those writes | of them after a > 1 h gap | text-only turns |h
| fable-day | fable | lead | 3 | 0.0195 | 9 | 3.4M | ''9'' | 8.7% |
| fable-day | opus | lead | 1 | 0.0125 | 4 | 1.7M | 4 | 9.1% |
| fable-day | sonnet | lead | 2 | ''0.0099'' | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0.5% |
| prior | sonnet | lead | 35 | ''0.0786'' | 671 | 271.8M | 30 | 1.9% |
| prior | opus | lead | 12 | 0.0735 | 159 | 79.8M | 4 | 4.0% |

* ''E1 reads PASS on the API meter.''
** The Sonnet leads' write:read ratio fell from 0.079 (5-minute TTL) to 0.010 under `subagentPromptCacheTtl: "1h"`, beating the &lt; 0.03 target. Cache writes fell from 64% of Sonnet lead $ to 22%.
** The plan-meter half of E1 (weekly Claude % per lane-day) stays unread here. My seat cannot see the plan meter.
* ''What a Fable lead still pays for in cache writes.''
** Every large rewrite on fable-day followed an idle gap longer than one hour: a lead waiting on a Terra seat or a CI vigil past the TTL.
** The 9 Fable rewrites wrote 3.4M tokens, about ''$68 at the $20 1h-write rate'', roughly a third of the $208 the three Fable leads cost.
** The fresh Founding-Wright made 0 such rewrites.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/3-outcomes-per-lead-today`>>

!! 3 · Outcomes per lead, today

Commits are the non-merge commits on the lead's lane branches, with committer time inside the lead's window ± 10 min. A red is a commit whose subject carries `red-` / `RED`.

| lead | tier | wall h | API-eq $ | commits | reds | $ / commit | PRs merged | Terra seats: full / partial / empty | what stood |h
| Walk-Wright | Fable | 19.2 | 94.5 | 11 | 3 | 8.6 | #115 (+ #122 open) | 0 / 1 / 2 | W4/W6 stood live: a face seated on a browser leaf and a Pixel-7 emulator |
| Mirror-Wright | Fable | 17.5 | 74.1 | 12 | 4 | 6.2 | #117 (part), #123, #124 | 3 / 2 / 2 | M1 + genesis re-bake + K1 passkey, all green |
| Founding-Wright | Fable (fresh) | 1.6 | 39.0 | 19 | 8 | ''2.1'' | none yet (fable-next) | 1 / 0 / 0 | W3/W8/W9/R4; the live walk measured 4 faults and cured 3 |
| Hive-Wright | Opus | 21.9 | 61.3 | 26 | 9 | 2.4 | #118 (+ #121 red, curing) | 1 / 2 / 1 | the content fence denies by default |
| Relay-Wright | Sonnet | 35.7 | 24.5 | 22 | 8 | ''1.1'' | #112 (+ i2-owed) | ''6 / 0 / 0'' | the far agent's relay seat; the census that found two real SharedWorker races |
| Porch-Wright | Sonnet | 17.0 | 16.3 | 19 | 0 | 0.9 | #114, #116, #119 | none | two porch slices + the boot-rest span cure |
| Test-Wright | Sonnet | 2.5 | 4.3 | 5 | 0 | 0.9 | #120 open, green | none | CI cells, weighted e2e shards |

''The same tokens repriced'' show how much each tier's price drives the bill. Each row prices one seat's actual tokens at the other tiers' rates (a different model would spend different tokens, so treat this as the price lever alone):

| seat | Fable rates | Opus rates | Sonnet rates |h
| Walk-Wright | ''94.5'' | 47.8 | 23.9 |
| Mirror-Wright | ''74.1'' | 39.6 | 19.8 |
| Founding-Wright | ''39.0'' | 22.1 | 11.0 |
| Hive-Wright | 106.5 | ''61.3'' | 30.6 |
| Relay-Wright | 82.1 | 49.1 | ''24.5'' |
| controller (main session, fable-day) | 114.9 | ''76.1'' | 38.0 |

On these leads Fable costs ''1.7–2.0× Opus'', not the 2.5× its list prices suggest. The reason: Fable's cache hit costs $0.25 against Opus's $0.20 (1.25×), and cache reads carry a large share of a waiting lead's bill. For a cache-read-heavy seat such as the controller, Fable comes to 1.5× Opus.

''Era totals'' (Claude subagents only; the controller is excluded):

| | prior (10-17 to 10-29 07:00Z) | fable-day |h
| Claude subagent API-eq $ | 1,869 over 86 seats | 345 over 29 seats |
| PRs merged in the era | 50 (+107,943 lines) | 10 (+12,304 lines), with 3 open PRs and 19 unlanded fable-next commits |
| $ per merged PR | ~37 | ~35 |

Per-PR cost barely moved. Most of the 1h-TTL savings went into Fable lead premiums. PRs differ in size and difficulty, so this is a coarse read, not a verdict.

''The controller seat today'' (main session `0f26457f…`, Opus 5.5, entries since 10-29 07:00Z): 570 API calls; 347 Bash, 121 SendMessage, 17 Agent. Tokens: 301M cache-read, 1.13M 1h writes, 340k output. That is about ''$76 API-eq, 18% of the day's Claude total (~$421)'', and 79% of the controller's cost is cache reads of its long context.

<<~/ahu>>

