!! 4 · Codex seats today (spend.py `--since 2026-10-29`, plus seat dirs)

| model | seats | input (uncached) | cached | output | API-eq $ | yield |h
| `gpt-6.1-terra` (build, medium) | 21 | 1.09M | 17.9M | 106k | ''≈ 2.5'' | 11 full, 5 partial, 5 empty |
| `gpt-6.1-sol` (read, high) | 6 (1 retry) | 1.20M | 23.4M | 93k | ''≈ 5.7'' | 5 of 5 finished reads carried a HIGH or BLOCKER the lead acted on; 1 seat died at capacity |
| `gpt-6-luna` (read, high) | 10 | 0.67M | 6.8M | 85k | ''≈ 0.18'' | 1 blocker, 1 HIGH, 1 MED (later a real race), several should-fix and LOW, 1 clean |

The Codex pool stands at 49% used of a 7-day window that resets 2026-11-04 (above the 20% floor). The pool percent, not API-eq, is the true Codex constraint.

''Terra yield by lead'', with each slice's nature from `plan.md`:
* ''Sonnet Relay-Wright:'' 6 of 6 full. The slices were listed census tests and fixes, mechanical.
* ''Fable Mirror-Wright:'' 3 of 7 full. Its M1 reds and fixes were judgment-heavy, with first passes at 3/10.
* ''Opus Hive-Wright:'' 1 of 4 full. One seat stalled on a stale dist, one died, one partial.
* ''Fable Walk-Wright:'' 0 of 3 full. Walk slices are integration judgment, and two seats were inspection-only.
* ''Fable Founding-Wright:'' 1 of 1 full. A tight fixture sweep.

Yield tracks the slice's nature, not the lead's tier.

''Findings caught before land'', each traced to `plan.md`:
# ''Sol HIGH (i2-owed):'' the vessel registers unproved sibling plane URLs, so a forged circles/identities URL passes. Closed before the push.
# ''Sol HIGH (i2-relay sol-6):'' the final admission check can use stale authority. It became slice-4 reds and a fix (`159ad140b` → `f2508ed59`).
# ''Sol HIGH ×2 (k19b):'' a label can launder synced content into mounted authority, and content can impersonate the mounted atom. These became `0d816bfff` ("RED (Luna and Sol, the slice's fresh read)") and its fix.
# ''Sol BLOCKER (fable-next):'' realm writers poison Kahu canon, because `foldRealmBags` trusts self-named stewards, and R4 derives canon from it. This is "R4's registry fault"; red `c2d7f8ee1` stands.
# ''Two real SharedWorker races (i2-owed):'' Terra wrote the census reds. The first race came from the census: `shared-holder.worker.ts` awaits its import before the connect listener. Luna's MED, that the census misses the lararium-web shims, led to the second (`void import(...)` in the web shim), which the lead confirmed.
# ''Luna blocker (d3 s6):'' default bag writes accept system titles. Luna should-fix (fable-next): a layer MOVE can delete a newer source version.

''Wasted or thin'', each cited in `plan.md`:
* 5 empty Terra build seats, four of them on judgment work, the fifth (Hive `terra-reds4b`) dead with no final.
* 1 Terra seat (Hive `terra-reds4`) that met a stale dist and proved none of its reds.
* 1 Sol seat that died at model capacity.
* 8 cancelled lane-branch CI runs from the queue clog.
* About 32.5 idle hours (gaps over 5 minutes) across the three Fable leads, of which the gaps over an hour cost ~$68 in cache rewrites.
* The seat-wall escape through `auto_review` (cured in `codex-seat.sh`; it cost a re-check, not a fault).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/caveats`>>

!! Caveats

* ''Small samples.'' Three Fable leads, one Opus lead today, two to three Sonnet leads today. No row here is a law. One lane-day per seat at most.
* ''Lanes are not comparable work.'' The Fable lanes held the founding walk and the mirror realm, the two most integration-dense lanes on the road. Porch and Test held mechanical work. Cost per commit flatters the mechanical lanes.
* ''Commit attribution'' by committer time can mis-assign a commit made by a Terra seat (one walk seat committed itself) or one carried by a merge. Walk and Founding overlap on `fable-next`; the dedupe gives each commit to whichever lead counted it first.
* ''Hidden thinking'' is inferred, not read. Per-block token counts are not logged.
* ''API-eq $ is not the plan meter.'' Max meters a five-hour window, a weekly window and a separate weekly Fable limit, and neither Anthropic nor OpenAI publishes a conversion.
* Prior-era Sonnet costs carry the 5-minute TTL penalty, which the house already cured. Compare tiers within an era, not across eras.

<<~/ahu>>

